              "lowMinutes": 30,
              "likelyMinutes": 45,
              "highMinutes": 60
            },
            "timeboxMinutes": 45,
            "commitment": {
              "category": "COMMITTED"
            },
            "hardDependencies": []
          }
        ],
        "decisions": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The learner has no prior demonstrated readiness for Ohm's law or series circuits.",
            "The accepted outcome is limited to one simple series circuit and does not require parallel circuits, power calculations, or complex networks."
          ],
          "tradeOffs": [
            "No separate relearning or practice set is included because the integrated activity already provides explanation, supported application, and independent changed-example evidence.",
            "No timed technique or paper analysis is included because there is no assessment or deadline."
          ],
          "unresolvedUncertainty": [
            "The learner's current familiarity with basic algebra and circuit vocabulary is unknown; the activity includes the needed rule and a worked example to make it self-contained."
          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop once the learner solves and explains the changed circuit independently; do not add further practice or checks unless the independent attempt fails."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "sharedDependencies": [],
  "tradeOffExplanation": "The accepted outcome is narrow and has no deadline or assessment, so the plan uses one integrated activity rather than separate learn, practice, and check stages. This sacrifices extra practice breadth and any timed technique, but preserves the full requirement: explaining Ohm's law and independently solving one changed simple series circuit. If the independent changed-circuit attempt fails, a bounded contingent remediation can be added later; it is not booked now because the integrated task may already meet the goal cleanly."
}

